cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the manuscript and its underlying context-shaping work."
title: "A Computed Preimage of 20-Round SHA-256 with Standard Padding for a Prescribed Structured Digest"
type: generic
authors:
  - family-names: Basra
    given-names: Kameldip Singh
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0977-4614"
date-released: 2026-10-17
version: "1.0"
url: "https://github.com/kamb-code/sha256-r19-preimage"
abstract: >-
  An explicit 55-byte message matching a prescribed structured 256-bit digest
  under the first 20 rounds of SHA-256, with standard IV, schedule, constants,
  feed-forward, and message padding. Includes reproducible forward verification.
  The padded all-ones extension is unexecuted and no arbitrary-target runtime
  guarantee is claimed.
keywords:
  - SHA-256
  - reduced-round preimages
  - standard padding
  - context shaping
  - reproducible verification
